RAUC signing key and certificate for Tess update bundles

development.key.pem and development.cert.pem are a self-signed key pair
for development only: the private key is in this repository, so anyone
can sign a bundle that these images accept.

The build copies the certificate to /etc/rauc/keyring.pem in the main
image (post-build-main.sh) and signs tess-update.raucb with the key
(post-image-main.sh). For production, generate a key outside this
repository and point the build at it:

  TESS_RAUC_KEY=/path/to/key.pem TESS_RAUC_CERT=/path/to/cert.pem make

A board only accepts bundles signed with the key matching the
certificate in its running image, so switching keys needs one update
signed with the old key that installs an image with the new certificate.

The development pair was created with:

  openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:4096 -nodes -keyout development.key.pem \
          -out development.cert.pem -days 36500 \
          -subj "/O=Phyx/CN=Tess RAUC development"
